    "title": "How to watch March Madness. See Friday's NCAA tournament schedule",
    "text": "March 20, 2026, 1:01 p.m. ETDid you survive the first day of March Madness?Are you ready for a second helping because it's starting all over again. The NCAA Tournament continues March 20 with 16 games taking place all over the country.Here's a look at the second day of the Road to the Final Four.When do 2026 NCAA Tournament games start?The first game – Akron at Texas Tech – will tip off at 12:10 p.m. Games will continue throughout the day.What channels are 2026 NCAA Tournament games on?The NCAA Tournament games will be shown on CBS, TBS, TNT and truTV.When does Villanova play in the 2026 NCAA Tournament play?Villanova will open its tournament play against Utah State at 4:10 p.m. March 20 in San Diego. The game will be broadcast on TNT.What's today's 2026 NCAA Tournament schedule?Here's a look at the NCAA Tournament schedule for March 20:Akron vs. Texas Tech, 12:10 p.m., truTVSanta Clara vs. Kentucky, 12:15 p.m., CBSLIU vs. Arizona, 1:35 p.m., TNTWright State vs. Virginia, 1:50 p.m., TBSTennessee State vs. Iowa State, 2:50 p.m., CBSHofstra vs. Alabama, 3:15 p.m., truTVUtah State vs. Villanova, 4:10 p.m., TNTMiami (Ohio) vs. Tennessee, 4:25 p.m., 4:25 p.m., TBSIowa vs. Clemson, 6:50 p.m., TNTNorthern Iowa vs. St. John's, 7:10 p.m., CBSUCF vs. UCLA, 7:25 p.m., TBSQueens (NC) vs. Purdue, 7:35 p.m., truTVPrairie View A&M vs. Florida, 9:25 p.m., TNTCalifornia Baptist vs. Kansas, 9:45 p.m., CBSFurman vs. UConn, 10 p.m., TBSMissouri vs. Miami (Florida), 10:10 p.m., truTVStream select NCAA Tournament games with Fubo (free trial)How to stream March Madness games for freeFree March Madness streaming options: March Madness Live app | Fubo (free trial)There are two free streaming options for the Men's NCAA Tournament, aside from watching games that air nationally on CBS, which is a linear TV channel offering.The first option is Fubo, which carries CBS and offers a free trial to new subscribers. CBS will televise 21 games of this year's tournament.The other option is the March Madness Live app. Those who have CBS or one of the Turner Sports Networks channels — TBS, TNT and truTV — as part of their TV packages, they can sign into the March Madness Live app with their TV login credentials. The same will work for watching games on a laptop through the March Madness Live webpage on the NCAA website.March Madness streaming options: How to livestream NCAA Tournament gamesStreaming options: March Madness Live app | Sling TV | Fubo (free trial)Watch NCAA Tournament game on SlingIn addition to the March Madness Live app and Fubo, Sling TV is another streaming option for March Madness games. Sling TV is a streaming option for games that will appear on TBS, TNT and truTV.TBS will televise 21 games, while truTV will air or simulcast a total of 24 games throughout the tournament, and TNT will air or simulcast a total of 15 games. The Final Four and national championship will also air on TBS, meaning Sling TV and the March Madness Live app are the only streaming options for those two rounds of the Men's NCAA Tournament.",
